# Directories that contain skill directories (each holding a SKILL.md).
#
# install-skills.sh installs every skill found under these roots. Listing a
# sibling repository here is how its skills get installed and health-checked
# without committing anything to that repository — which matters for a fork:
# `ack-workspace refresh` does ResetHard + Clean + ResetHardTo upstream on the
# default branch, so a script committed to a fork's main is destroyed by a
# routine refresh, taking the protection with it.
#
# Paths are relative to this repository's root (or absolute; ~ and $VARS are
# expanded). Prefer relative: they are what makes the installation survive the
# checkout moving, since a re-run then resolves the new location on its own.
#
# A listed root that does not exist is reported and skipped, not an error — a
# sibling repo you have not cloned simply contributes no skills.

# This repository.
skills

# ACK development skills (upstream fork; we deliberately commit nothing to it).
../ack-dev-skills/skills
